"answer": "According to the provided documents, common causes of sciatica include a ruptured intervertebral disk (also referred to as a herniated disk), narrowing of the spinal canal known as spinal stenosis, and injuries such as a pelvic fracture [MLP-1532]. A herniated disk occurs when the jelly-like center of a disk leaks, irritating nearby nerves [MLP-284]. Additionally, the sources note that in many cases, no specific cause can be found [MLP-1532]."
